#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0537 expect=violation domain=DS
#note "Neither EPOCH nor DSSCAT is present. DSSCAT not_exists is satisfied (this is the DSSCAT-absent half of the sheet pair) and the EPOCH exists guard was REMOVED, so the key degrades to (DSCAT, USUBJID) and the duplicate subject is flagged. Pinned at 1 finding. This rule groups on [USUBJID, EPOCH]; EPOCH is absent and is dropped, leaving two USUBJID groups, so the fixture's ceiling is 2 - the pin discriminates 1 from 2, not from 3."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSCAT    type=Char label="Category for Disposition Event"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | DISPOSITION EVENT
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 2 | DISPOSITION EVENT
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1023 | 3 | DISPOSITION EVENT
---
